      "solution_status": "complete",
      "independent_solution": "Compare every adjacent ratio. (a) All four ratios are 1/10: geometric, q=1/10. (b) All three ratios are 1/10: geometric, q=1/10. (c) The ratios are 2,4,4,4,2, so it is not geometric. (d) All four ratios are -10: geometric, q=-10. (e) The ratios are 11/10,111/110,1111/1110, which are unequal, so it is not geometric. (f) 5^(k+1)/5^k=5 at each step: geometric, q=5. All listed first terms are nonzero; no nonexistent common ratio is assigned to (c) or (e).",
      "subquestions": [
        {"label": "a", "adjacent_ratios": ["1/10", "1/10", "1/10", "1/10"], "geometric": true, "q": "1/10"},
        {"label": "b", "adjacent_ratios": ["1/10", "1/10", "1/10"], "geometric": true, "q": "1/10"},
