    {
      "source_number": "272",
      "subquestion_count": 2,
      "solution_status": "complete",
      "independent_solution": "The displayed 3rd, 4th and 5th terms fix q and allow division backward. (a) q=36/24=54/36=3/2. Thus y_2=24/(3/2)=16 and y_1=16/(3/2)=32/3; the reconstructed start is 32/3,16,24,36,54. (b) q=-135/225=81/(-135)=-3/5. Thus y_2=225/(-3/5)=-375 and y_1=-375/(-3/5)=625; the reconstructed start is 625,-375,225,-135,81. Both known adjacent ratios agree in each part, and q is nonzero.",
